efits than either treatment alone", "takeaways": ["Up to 18% energy expenditure increase in mice without appetite suppression", "Preserves lean muscle mass, unlike GLP-1 drugs alone", "Enhanced results when combined with GLP-1 medications", "Findings published in Science Advances; human efficacy/safety not yet established"], "sources": [{"label": "ScienceDaily", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261118073918.htm", "origin": "research"}, {"label": "ScienceDaily — Health", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261118073918.htm", "origin": "rss"}, {"label": "ScienceDaily — Fitness", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261118073918.htm", "origin": "rss"}, {"label": "ScienceDaily — Nutrition", "url": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261118073918.htm", "origin": "rss"}], "subfeeds": [{"key": "diet-exercise", "title": "Diet & Exercise"}, {"key": "health", "title": "Health"}, {"key": "science", "title": "Science"}], "feeds": [{"key": "science", "title": "Science"}], "researched": true, "receivedAt": "2026-11-20T14:28:59.152065+00:00", "relatedTitle": "", "relatedUrl": "", "updatesTitle": "", "updatesUrl": ""}, {"title": "Ketogenic diet reduces liver fat by 67% in clinical trial", "url": "news/diet-exercise/2026-11-20/#ketogenic-diet-reduces-liver-fat-by-67-in-clinical-trial", "importance": 7, "date": "2026-11-20", "summary": "A clinical trial of 42 adults found the ketogenic diet reduced liver fat by an average of 67% over four to five months, substantially outperforming Mediterranean and low-fat diets despite similar weight loss across all groups. Approximately half of ketogenic diet participants no longer met diagnosti", "takeaways": ["67% average reduction in liver fat over 4–5 months on ketogenic diet", "~50% of ketogenic group no longer met prediabetes criteria", "Substantially outperformed Mediterranean and low-fat diets", "Study published in Cell Metabolism by Washington University School of Medicine